	(footprint "Optical:PD_FGA01FC_EdgeBracket"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "382050a9-24d0-42e3-a440-5fb43f9b063e")
		(at 226.65 106.538)
		(descr "Thorlabs FGA01FC InGaAs photodiode held by the photodiode_PCBedgeholder bracket (Bracket v5). The bracket clamps the PCB FRONT EDGE in a 1.86 mm slot and the diode flange bolts to its front face with 2x M2, so the board carries the diode and the panel only needs a clearance hole. ORIGIN = can axis projected onto the board; local +X points TOWARD the board front edge, which MUST sit at local X = +5.00 (see the F.Fab datum line). Can back face lands 1.0 mm forward of the edge. LEADS: pin 1 (K) and pin 3 (A) exit at the F.Cu surface plane at Y = +/-1.25 and lie FLAT on top - they solder to surface pads, no bend. Pin 2 (CASE) exits 1.25 mm below the axis, bends down across the 1.0 mm gap in front of the board edge, passes UNDER the board and solders to a B.Cu pad. Clocking pin 2 downward makes the flange orientation unique, which is what stops pin 1 and pin 3 being swapped. MOUNTING: 2x plated 2.2 mm holes (ISO 273 close clearance for M2 - FINISHED hole size, tell the fab) on 13.624 mm centres, 2.5 mm in from the board edge, carried as pad 2 so they land on the CASE/GND net with no schematic change. Their 4.0 x 5.0 mm mask-free lands are the metal-to-metal contact face for the conductive bracket arms - specify ENIG, a HASL bump makes a poor contact. VERIFY the pin 1 / pin 3 assignment against the physical part before build: the datasheet gives only a schematic symbol and a bottom view, no pin table.")
		(tags "photodiode InGaAs TO-46 FC/PC Thorlabs FGA01FC edge bracket panel mount grounded")
